# member_const_cross_ns_pub_inherit.tkr — a NAMESPACE-IDENTITY project-regressor (0.3.1
# regressor-principal, §5 triage exception): a `pub` member const's visibility REACHES across
# namespaces, including through an inheriting subclass declared in a different namespace
# (`sub`). Needs a real second namespace distinct from the root; flattening would collapse the
# boundary the assertion depends on (a vacuous pass — the `pub`-reaches-across-namespaces
# claim is untestable with only one namespace left). Kept on disk, unflattened; not
# inline-scenario-izable.

Feature: member_const_cross_ns_pub_inherit — a pub member const reaches across namespaces through an inheriting subclass

  Scenario: sub's Sub class, inheriting Base, legally reads Base's pub const from the sub namespace
    When built and run
    Then exit = 42
